// @corpus: rejected
// @id: R-115
// @category: a predicate with a body required where it is not seen
// @rule: PW6925
// @invariant: predicate_answered_by_its_body
// @charter: §7.8, §9.2
// @milestone: 14
// @expect-error: `requires WroteLetter` names no predicate `LetterEdits` sees, and `Letters` gives `WroteLetter` a body: the host would ask the deployment for it instead
//
// Track `row-ownership` (the review's finding 4): A-055's `WroteLetter` has a
// body, and this module imports `Letters` for its id alone. Its `requires`
// named no component, so the host asked the deployment for `WroteLetter`,
// whose predicate of that name, if any, answered in the body's place.

module LetterEdits

import Letters.{ LetterId }

command edit(id: LetterId) -> ()
    requires    WroteLetter(id)
    transaction serializable
{
    ()
}
